## Baseline measurements

{{PERFORMANCE_BASELINE}}

Record representative small, module-local, cross-module, and public-contract
tasks. Measure at least selected files/bytes, tool calls, elapsed time, checks,
rework, and observed token usage when the active Codex surface exposes it.

## Paired A/B study

Use the repository A/B analyzer only with paired runs of the same real task,
base revision, model configuration, environment, and acceptance checks. Arm A
uses the target's original guidance or the prior strict/full workflow; arm B
uses the tiered/core workflow. Record first-pass success, user round trips,
elapsed seconds, input/output/total tokens when available, scope escapes, and
review defects. Missing telemetry remains missing and is never treated as zero.

- First-pass success means all predeclared acceptance checks pass before
  user-directed rework.
- User round trips count requests for clarification, approval, correction, or
  missing input after the initial task.
- Scope escapes count writes or attempted writes outside the authorized class
  boundary; review defects count distinct actionable P0-P3 findings.
- Elapsed time and token telemetry must come from the same measurement method in
  both arms.

Example or synthetic records validate the analyzer but are not performance
evidence. Report sample size, incomplete pairs, configuration mismatches, and
metric deltas; do not claim causality from unpaired or confounded runs.

## Quality guardrails

{{QUALITY_GUARDRAILS}}

Token or time reductions are regressions when they reduce boundary compliance,
consumer/contract coverage, verification coverage, first-pass success, or
review defect detection.

## Task and reasoning classes

- L1: declared local, public-contract-preserving change with known verification;
  a direct implementation request authorizes execution.
- L2: module-local behavior or debugging inside once-approved directories.
- L3: cross-module, compatibility, concurrency, or data-flow change with an
  exact approved plan.
- L4: architecture, security/privacy, migration, destructive/external, or
  high-cost failure work with complete impact and rollback evidence.

The operator selects the model and reasoning level. Repository guidance records
task complexity and evidence; it does not pin a changing product/model name.

## Parallelism budget

Parallel work requires explicit approval, stable interfaces, non-overlapping
write scopes, and one integrating owner. Report wall-clock savings separately
from total agent/token consumption.

